{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3901","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3901","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3901\",\"parent_revision\":\"f6d559feb673ac746f65459cf2848045a2f22c74fbdfd8a241845349907f1751\",\"root_revision\":\"f6d559feb673ac746f65459cf2848045a2f22c74fbdfd8a241845349907f1751\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nEnsure that a fact-check result produced by DH remains consumable by grooming finalization and can be matched to the original hypothesis without changing its verdict or evidence. This is the smallest bounded improvement identified during the OMS comparison: correct one existing producer/consumer handoff, rather than add another orchestration system.\\n\\n**OBSERVED \u2014 source-contract discrepancy on main:** At `9dc96e51be1f277345207c8d9664c17ecda2b095`, `agents/fact-checker.md` Step 4 prescribes uppercase `CLAIM:`, `VERDICT:`, and `EVIDENCE:` fields; Step 5 instructs the agent to persist that block verbatim. The grooming swarm instead specifies lowercase `verdict:`, `claim:`, `evidence:`, and `source:`. Its hypothesis contract requires `claim: HYPOTHESIS: <exact original text>`, while finalization requires a `verdict:` field and uses exact hypothesis text to associate results with their originating claims.\\n\\n**DERIVED consequence:** An agent can follow its own output instructions and still violate the downstream contract. Correct verification can become unusable to finalization or unmatchable to its hypothesis, causing avoidable retries or leaving the hypothesis unresolved. This is established by source/contract inspection; no live grooming failure was reproduced for this item.\\n\\nPR #3887's pending skill/adapter extraction also leaves this handoff under-specified, as noted in its P1 review. The discrepancy is already present on main and should not be described as caused solely by that extraction. Work on this item should coordinate with #3887 rather than produce competing fixes.\\n\\n### Required behavior\\n\\nThe DH-facing result must satisfy the existing grooming field contract before persistence. Preserve each original claim's identity, every hypothesis's exact text, the VERIFIED/REFUTED/INCONCLUSIVE distinction, evidence, and source attribution. Internal claim analysis must not replace the identity used by downstream matching. Missing evidence remains INCONCLUSIVE; malformed or missing results must not be accepted as successful verification.\\n\\nKeep reusable factual-verification methodology independent of DH's serialization and persistence contract. Ad-hoc verification without a backlog item must not acquire backlog side effects. In grooming mode the fact-checker remains authorized to write only its Fact-Check section, not item lifecycle state.\\n\\n### Reproduce the contract conflict\\n\\n1. Read the pinned fact-checker Step 4 and Step 5: the uppercase example is explicitly the content to persist.\\n2. Compare it with the pinned swarm's Fact-Checker output contract and finalization's minimum-content gate.\\n3. Compare hypothesis identity requirements with the producer's output instructions. Record the discrepancy without claiming that a model or executable parser has already failed in a live run.\\n\\n## Fact-Check\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nverdict: VERIFIED\\nclaim: The pinned fact-checker instructs uppercase output and verbatim persistence.\\nevidence: Step 4's emitted field names are CLAIM, VERDICT, EVIDENCE, CROSS_CHECK, EXPLANATION and CITATION; Step 5 persists the full block unchanged. The local structural regression fails because claim/evidence/source/verdict are absent as lowercase top-level fields.\\nsource: plugins/development-harness/agents/fact-checker.md at 2e7b66e575f2d4b6b7a518e267618db3dc1b885b; source blob 7308874b51bfa3db5f4d8f40e24c3fc9049ea12b.\\n\\nverdict: VERIFIED\\nclaim: Grooming requires lowercase result fields and exact original hypothesis text.\\nevidence: swarm.md defines verdict/claim/evidence/source and HYPOTHESIS identity; finalize.md matches each hypothesis independently and preserves an INCONCLUSIVE marker.\\nsource: plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/references/workflows/groom/swarm.md and finalize.md at the same revision; source blobs 85c7bb02f215b16a0c7a1e0105e5825bc7a4f4a9 and 690d0855fae7f38177fa124f97dd42a981de3193.\\n\\nverdict: INCONCLUSIVE\\nclaim: The source-contract mismatch causes a live model-driven grooming failure.\\nevidence: unavailable \u2014 the executed reproduction inspects real Markdown producer/consumer contracts; no authenticated fresh-agent execution or DH backlog service is available in this session. No live grooming run was executed.\\nsource: unavailable \u2014 no live-run trace exists; structural test evidence is not a substitute.\\n</div>\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nRT-ICA Final: Fact-Check producer and grooming consumers specify incompatible result formats\\nDate: 2026-09-25\\nGoal: Preserve a factual result's identity, evidence and verdict through the existing DH grooming handoff.\\n\\nConditions:\\n1. Required outcome and scope | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: issue Description and Acceptance Criteria; user's request to groom and implement as a new PR.\\n2. Exact producer and consumer contracts | Snapshot: DERIVABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: pinned agent/swarm/finalize sources and failing source-contract reproduction.\\n3. Protected research, write-authority and hypothesis-resolution behavior | Snapshot: DERIVABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: full producer and finalizer reads at 2e7b66e.\\n4. Concurrent-work boundary | Snapshot: DERIVABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: #3887 remains open at 32b53d1835e2fa5c6371782b8f75652554e18f11; this issue is independent of its merge.\\n5. Available validation and its limits | Snapshot: DERIVABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: Python/pytest/Markdown parser available; direct git clone fails DNS; no fresh-agent CLI/credentials. Source blobs were reconstructed locally and checked against Git object IDs.\\n\\nDecision: APPROVED-FOR-PLANNING\\n\\nTool limitations are known verification boundaries, not invented missing product requirements. They do not authorize reporting a live evaluation as passed.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Issue Classification\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nType: defect\\n\\nRationale: the producer's explicit serialization instructions disagree with its actual consumers; correcting only the visible casing would leave claim identity and validation obligations underspecified.\\n\\nAnalysis Method: bounded producer \u2192 persisted section \u2192 consumer contract trace. No historical author intent or unobserved runtime cause is inferred.\\n\\nScenario Target: a source-supported result following the producer's instructions should be usable by grooming and match the original claim without changing its verdict or losing evidence.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Impact Radius\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n### Systems Inventory\\n\\n| Surface | Role and connection | Consequence / verification obligation |\\n| --- | --- | --- |\\n| `agents/fact-checker.md` | Producer and persistence adapter | Preserve tool-backed research, CoVe, source excerpts, dates, ad-hoc behavior, memory restrictions and Fact-Check-only writes while emitting a consumable result. |\\n| `skills/work-backlog-item/references/workflows/groom/swarm.md` | Dispatch and result-contract consumer | Preserve claim coverage and RT-ICA verdict mapping; remove conflicting result examples on this path. |\\n| `skills/work-backlog-item/references/workflows/groom/finalize.md` | Validation and hypothesis-resolution consumer | Validate claimed results before using them; preserve single-hypothesis RCA precedence, exact multiple-hypothesis mapping, unrelated lines and update-before-sync ordering. |\\n| DH bundled result reference | Shared contract surface | Remain reachable within an installed DH bundle, not through a repository-only path; do not absorb universal research methodology or lifecycle ownership. |\\n| DH contract tests and behavior scenarios | Verification | Distinguish static schema/routing checks from actual agent/persistence behavior. Cover positive, negative, uncertain and malformed returns. |\\n| DH plugin manifest | Distribution | Version change required for installed users to receive the corrected instructions. |\\n| PR #3887 | Concurrent agent-to-skill extraction | Carry the same DH-owned result contract forward rather than restoring an unconstrained 'complete verdict' handoff. |\\n\\n### Excluded Candidates / Unknown Frontier\\n\\nBackend storage, MCP/CLI schemas, schedulers, work-ledger lifecycle and unrelated agent conversions are excluded: this issue supplies no evidence that those need redesign. Model adherence, installed-harness navigation and live persistence remain unexecuted evidence boundaries. Existing stored history is not silently rewritten.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Dependencies\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nNo upstream implementation dependency. Coordinate the result-contract ownership with #3887. Do not merge that PR or modify its branch as part of this issue.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Priority\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nP1 retained from the item.\\nEffort: Small, bounded instruction/contract correction plus focused regression evidence. Live comparative agent evaluation remains a separate validation lane, not a claimed zero-cost activity.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Design Intent Alignment\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAlignment assessment: ALIGNED\\n\\nBasis: the issue's required behavior and DH AGENTS.md's logical handoff/ownership rules. A reusable analysis process can remain independent of the DH serialization contract. Restoring compatibility does not authorize a new workflow, broader fact-checking, or changing who may mutate lifecycle state.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Producer and consumer agree on one reachable DH Fact-Check contract, including exact hypothesis identity; no conflicting output instructions remain on this path.\\n- [ ] Ordinary claims and multiple distinct hypotheses retain their verdicts and match the correct originating text after the producer-to-persistence-to-consumer handoff.\\n- [ ] Evidence covers VERIFIED, REFUTED, INCONCLUSIVE, missing evidence, and malformed/missing output against the actual finalization and hypothesis-resolution contracts, not only an isolated producer example.\\n- [ ] Reusable verification behavior, ad-hoc use, and existing write-authority boundaries remain intact. Any unexecuted behavioral checks are explicitly identified.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Expected Behavior\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nEach dispatched claim keeps its original identity independently of analytical narrowing. Results retain supported verdicts and evidence. Unavailable evidence is explicitly INCONCLUSIVE, never a fabricated source or successful verification. Missing/invalid verdicts and ambiguous identities do not resolve hypotheses. Ad-hoc calls return results without backlog writes; grooming writes only the permitted section. Existing RCA precedence and finalization write order remain intact.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Reproducibility\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nA focused pytest probe loads the actual pinned producer Step 4 and the swarm's output template through a Markdown parser. It compares emitted field names with the consumer's required fields. Result before edits: one failing test; producer keys `CITATION, CLAIM, CROSS_CHECK, EVIDENCE, EXPLANATION, VERDICT`, missing lowercase `claim, evidence, source, verdict`.\\n\\nThe three local source snapshots were byte-verified against their Git blob IDs. This reproduces the source-contract discrepancy only. No real production issue was mutated to test an agent's behavior.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a DH user, I need a verified claim to reach the next workflow stage with its identity and evidence intact, so that grooming does not repeat valid work or lose the connection between a hypothesis and its result.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Agent task - auto-derived from input; user requested the smallest useful DH improvement following the OMS assessment.\\n- **Priority**: P1 \u2014 the same required handoff is identified as P1 in the linked review; this priority does not assert a reproduced production incident.\\n- **Type**: Bug.\\n- **Added**: 2026-09-25.\\n- **Creation classification**: BEHAVIORAL/PROCESS; the behavior requirements above are preserved, not an implementation plan.\\n- **Duplicate check**: Searched Fact-Check contract, fact-checker adapter, hypothesis matching, and references to #3887. No equivalent standalone item was identified. #3268 concerns dispatch input/anchoring rather than persisted result compatibility; #995 concerns implementation contracts rather than this grooming result format.\\n- **Workflow stage**: Grooming assessments recorded below; implementation authorized by the user's request. GitHub MCP is the available backend interface. No DH `backlog_groom` call or independent grooming swarm is claimed.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Root-Cause Analysis\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n**Root cause**: independently maintained output specifications disagree on the same handoff. `agents/fact-checker.md` prescribes an uppercase block and verbatim persistence, while `groom/swarm.md` requires lowercase fields and exact hypothesis identity. `groom/finalize.md` consumes the latter. This is an observed interface/representation defect, not evidence that verification methodology itself is wrong.\\n\\nThe producer's permission to narrow a vague assertion does not distinguish analysis scope from the original identity used by consumers. The consumer's minimum-content check mentions only presence of `verdict:`, despite the fuller swarm contract. These are adjacent obligations of the same handoff; preserving exact identity and refusing malformed positive verdicts are part of the existing issue requirements.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-09-25)\\n\\n## Evidence\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [Original main fact-checker: exact output and verbatim persistence](https://github.com/Jamie-BitFlight/claude_skills/blob/9dc96e51be1f277345207c8d9664c17ecda2b095/plugins/development-harness/agents/fact-checker.md).\\n- [Original main grooming consumer: Fact-Checker output contract](https://github.com/Jamie-BitFlight/claude_skills/blob/9dc96e51be1f277345207c8d9664c17ecda2b095/plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/references/workflows/groom/swarm.md#fact-checker-output-contract).\\n- [Original main finalization: output validation and hypothesis resolution](https://github.com/Jamie-BitFlight/claude_skills/blob/9dc96e51be1f277345207c8d9664c17ecda2b095/plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/references/workflows/groom/finalize.md).\\n- [Related P1 review on PR #3887](https://github.com/Jamie-BitFlight/claude_skills/pull/3887#discussion_r4099564317).\\n</div>\\n\\n## Validation Boundary\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nRequired comparison: existing source-contract reproduction versus corrected sources, bundled reference reachability, and conservation of unaffected workflow sections. Behavioral scenarios cover ordinary claims, multiple similar hypotheses, REFUTED/INCONCLUSIVE results, missing evidence, malformed results, RCA precedence, ad-hoc use and write failures. Authored scenarios are not passing runs; preserve that distinction in the PR and completion report.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Implementation Progress\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nNew PR: #3906 \u2014 `fix/dh-fact-check-handoff-3901`, initial commit `c80421738428c4f8c48a78f8579040869973dbe1`, test-hygiene correction `e2c3eb299a59d58dad9f2244e627d909c4119a60`.\\n\\n- [x] Manual grooming and a separate implementation plan recorded before publishing.\\n- [x] Shared bundled result contract and producer/consumer instructions implemented.\\n- [x] Original schema failure reproduced; candidate's seven structural tests pass locally.\\n- [x] Protected research, authority, RCA and final write-back sections compared with the original.\\n- [x] Eight behavioral cases and their baseline/candidate execution protocol authored, explicitly not executed.\\n- [x] Version-only DH/Codex/Cursor manifest updates published.\\n- [ ] Final CI/review and live behavioral evidence accepted; no merge or issue closure performed.\\n\\nThe initial CI run passed manifest sync/version checks, Markdown lint, plugin validation, integration and both cross-backend lanes. It found new-test lint/type defects; those were corrected in `e2c3eb2` and the seven local tests rerun successfully. The newest CI run, rather than the initial result, determines current readiness. Full review-cycle certification remains unavailable without the receiving-pr-reviews CLI's canonical snapshot ingress; raw MCP review inspection is diagnostic only.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"f06a2890f6c19c33313bbe0874de9df867be3d94d0e010dd34ad4bb0d5977ea5\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABXCLLjw\"}"}